import ../../../testing/driver.dl

document navigation test:
    tab group "Tabs" using no UI appearance:
        tab "First":
            paragraph "First panel" using no UI appearance
        tab "Second":
            paragraph "Second panel" using no UI appearance
        tab "Third":
            paragraph "Third panel" using no UI appearance
    tool field "One" sized 100:
        menu item "One"
        menu item "Two"
        menu item "Three"

set instance to an instance of navigation test
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 400 by 260 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view the address of view
set the "Second" control in (the address of instance) enabled false
ignore update UI view the address of view
set view's focus order to 1
set view's keyboard focus to true
refresh UI focus in (the address of view)
set view's key press to 262
navigate UI tabs in (the address of view)
require condition ((the value of "Tabs" in (the address of instance)) = 2) reporting "Arrow navigation selected a disabled tab"
set the "First" control in (the address of instance) enabled false
set the "Third" control in (the address of instance) enabled false
ignore update UI view the address of view
set group to view's layout's first
require condition (group's order = 0) reporting "A disabled tab group retained a stale focus order"
set field to group's next
activate UI layout field in (the address of view)
set two to the UI child at 1 in (field's node)
set UI control two enabled false in (the address of instance)
set view's key press to 264
ignore process UI control popup input in (the address of view)
require condition (view's popup choices' selected = 2) reporting "Arrow navigation selected a disabled popup item"
set UI control (field's node) enabled false in (the address of instance)
set view's key press to 257
ignore process UI control popup input in (the address of view)
require condition ((the UI value for (field's node) in (the address of instance))'s number = 0) reporting "An open disabled field accepted a menu item"
require condition (view's popup = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "A disabled popup owner remained open"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Disabled tabs and popup items are skipped, and an open disabled field cannot change."
